    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "After World War II, Neukölln fell under the American sector before becoming part of West Berlin in 1949.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuk%C3%B6lln"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Since the late 1950s, Neukölln has had one of Berlin’s highest shares of immigrant residents, especially in its northern industrial areas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuk%C3%B6lln"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "An influx of students and artists since the mid‑2000s has sparked gentrification across Neukölln’s urban quarters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuk%C3%B6lln"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hermannplatz station in Neukölln serves as a major interchange for the U7, U8, and S‑bahn lines.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
